WEBVTT

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.530
Ow!

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.740
What?

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.660
Someone's there!

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.880
Who?

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.710
Someone next door was spying on us.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.370
Okay, you.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.760
Let's see how <i>you</i> like being spied on!

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.760
Found you!

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.390
Whoa!

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.210
What?

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.040
What are you doing?!

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:12.940
Are you okay?

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.780
Help...

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.480
Someone help!

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.780
Be careful!

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.210
Tetsuko!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.510
You okay, man?

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.630
She almost got me killed!

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.320
Tetsuko!

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.700
Pizza's here.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.520
Coming!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.710
What's with all the trash?

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.410
Fresh air.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.120
Kinda plain, huh?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.660
Looks like their uniforms are sailor suits.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.900
I have to wear that?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.640
Ew.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.080
Hello?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.320
Yes?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:39.800
This is my daughter, Tetsuko Arisugawa.
 She's in ninth grade.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.100
I'd like to enroll her here.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.340
Transferring?

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.100
Yes, that's right.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.890
The principal is out right now. Let me see.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.890
What are these?

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.570
Snails.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.210
Y-You like snails?

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.580
They're for the students.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.890
You'll need a transfer request.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.080
Did you bring it?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.000
I'll also need your old school ID.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.490
How do I get those?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.510
You'll have to go to city hall first.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.830
Have you not been there yet?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:15.350
I was thinking I'd go when I'm more settled.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.120
You should make it a priority.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.070
Do you have your daughter's old student ID?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.150
No.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.180
Oh, I do.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.780
I have it.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.720
Then please go to city hall and get a transfer request.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.590
Of course!

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.040
Fine.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.870
Once you've gotten that, come back here.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.500
When I have the documents I can give you your textbooks and catch-up material.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.450
Also, you'll have to buy a school uniform and gym clothes from the school store.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.210
With luck she can be in class by the afternoon.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.450
That's great!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.340
Thank you!

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:46.870
And...

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.180
Eh, it'll be fine.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.700
Sir, what's your name?

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:50.910
Yes?

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.110
Tomonaga. I teach science.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.080
Thank you, Mr. Tomonaga.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.140
He's so handsome!

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.790
Wouldn't it be great to be in his class, Tetsuko?

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.050
Ew.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.160
This is Satomi Ogino. She's a homeroom teacher for the ninth grade.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.570
I also teach language arts.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:10.530
What?

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.840
You're not her homeroom teacher, Mr. Tomonaga?

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.290
What a shame.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.370
Feel free to ask me anything.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:24.110
The uniform store was sold out and won't have any more for a while.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.770
Can I wear this until then?

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.060
Sure, sure.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.540
That's just fine.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.680
Hey, are you dating Mr. Tomonaga?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.330
Stop it!

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.250
No, no! We're not dating.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.340
Really?

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.900
You seemed close.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.150
Stop it, Mommy!

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.890
Oh, look at her!

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.900
Still calling me Mommy!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.580
So, what?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.610
Going to be mean again?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.610
Just get out of here!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.270
Stop that, Tetsuko—

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.360
This is our classroom.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.040
Go!

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.920
Good luck!

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.330
Okay, everyone!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.340
We've got a new friend joining us.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.190
Be nice.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:08.150
Now, I'm sure you're all wondering what the new student's name is.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.480
Write it on the board for everyone, please.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.140
Then introduce yourself.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.290
I'm Tetsuko Arisugawa. Nice to meet you.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:41.460
I hope everyone can see that.
 Remember, everyone, be nice.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.370
'Kay.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.670
Sit at the empty desk.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.330
Oh, Ms. Arisugawa. The one in front.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.870
Goodbye!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:16.870
See ya.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.230
I'm in group two.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.940
We have clean-up duty this week, right?

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.970
Oh, uh...

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.220
Thanks.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.430
There.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.410
God.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:42.780
Stop!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.020
Don't touch that one!

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.000
Don't touch that either!

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.410
What the hell?

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:06.720
Hey.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.910
What's this?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.450
How was school?

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.070
Sucky.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.640
Sucky?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.440
Why?

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.020
Bullies?

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:28.810
Bullies?

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:29.820
Why?

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.210
Did you do something?

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.160
In a day? Yeah, totally.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.360
Maybe it's the new kid treatment.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.770
It'll pass.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.790
You'll make friends soon.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.270
I remember that happened to me.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.290
When all the guys like you, the girls hate you.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.360
That was <i>you?</i>

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.650
I was as pretty as a pop star back then.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.260
Didn't have any girl friends.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:02.560
Not that I needed any.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.120
Nope, nope.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.610
Just a waste of time.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:13.340
It was always my dream to have my picture taken by Kishin Shinoyama.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.830
Excuse me!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.170
Yes?

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.610
Non-burnable trash is Wednesdays!

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.230
Sorry.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.360
Honestly, have you no sense?

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.070
Toodle-oodle-oo!

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.730
Give it back!

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.400
Indirect kiss time!

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.530
Please, no! Just give it back!

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.370
Toodle-oodle-oo!

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.370
Give it back, Chiba!

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.280
Give it back!

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:05.410
Ow!

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.440
Hey, Chiba! You okay?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.040
He's totally broken something!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.500
It's not my fault.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.220
I didn't do it!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.460
Here.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:15.760
Oh, thanks.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.460
Take it.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:19.650
I don't want it.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.000
Then throw it away.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.030
Hi, Kuro!

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:40.220
Wow! How long's it been?

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:42.940
Who're you?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.720
Huh? You don't remember me?

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:49.320
We were in the same class back in Hasegawa Ballet.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.630
Oh, Fuko!

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.540
You go here?

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.750
What're you doing here?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.160
I'm the transfer student that transferred in.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:11.470
If you're looking for a book, this place probably has it.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.040
Wow, talk about creepy.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.600
That's actually kind of cool.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:20.980
Kuro!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:25.090
This is the one your mom wrote, right?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.450
Oh, wow.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:32.240
This place is certainly something if they've got a book that rare.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.320
Thank you for your purchase.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:38.250
I'll be returning it now.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.780
Oh, that's Kappa Sanpeido.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.060
It's good.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.610
No kidding. I'm drooling.

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:46.720
Wanna try?

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.560
Sorry, I've got lessons.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:52.340
Ballet?

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.480
Yep.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.850
You're still doing that?

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.280
What about you?

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.660
I did.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.060
But I probably won't anymore.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:01.500
Why?

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.980
Do it with me.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.940
Maybe I'll ask my mom.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.340
Budget's pretty tight, though.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:12.120
That's such a shame, Kuro.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.420
Hey, how about just coming to watch?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.810
Right now.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.640
Here we are.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.380
So old!

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.450
Watch your back!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.620
Sorry I'm late!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.270
Mademoiselle, do you have a second?

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:37.080
This is an old classmate, Tetsuko Kuro—

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.230
Tetsuko Arisugawa.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.530
You've practiced ballet?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.190
For how long?

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.110
Uh, seven years.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.610
Really? Would you like to join?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.820
No, no! I'm just watching—

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.370
What's your shoe size?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.200
Lucky you, huh, Kuro?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.790
Rock, paper, scissors, Spock!

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.030
Winner-winner chicken dinner!

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.710
I lost...

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.650
Geez!

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.410
Just kill me, Kuro!

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.530
God!

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.590
Did your name change, Kuro?

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:37.420
Yeah. It's Arisugawa, not Kuroyanagi.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.600
So stop calling me Kuro.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.060
Okay.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.150
Arisugawa's a cute name.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.700
Can I call you Alice?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.090
Alice?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.820
Alice is cute.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:51.700
But why'd it change?

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.430
Divorce?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.340
Don't pry, Fu.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.080
Well, this is my place.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:03.880
What?

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.220
Here?

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:08.270
Next to the flower house?

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.990
Flower house?

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:13.720
We call this house the flower house.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.640
The flower house?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:22.650
There's always someone watching people from that window.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:25.670
It's super creepy.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.640
Look! That one!

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.760
Stop!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.560
They could be watching!

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.860
Wait, wrong way—

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:46.700
Please, just stay with me!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.720
Why're you crying?

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.410
Wipe your eyes, big girl.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.370
What're you doing?

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:10.050
Do you know what time it is?

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:18.430
I went to a ballet studio today so I felt like dancing.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.320
A ballet studio?

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.390
Way out here?

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:23.150
It's pretty legit.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.400
You wanna join?

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.860
You should!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:32.240
Yeah, but with what money?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.490
That's not something you should worry about!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.700
Tetsuko.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:41.980
Money's meant to be spent.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.820
How have you survived all these years?

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:50.180
Money is meant to be spent!

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.700
Alice, do you attend Ishinomori Middle?

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.740
Yeah.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.900
Just like Fu.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:02.190
Have you heard of the murder?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.180
Huh?

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.500
Murder?

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.940
The Ishinomori Murder!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.040
You don't?

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.360
So you don't.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.410
What? Tell me?

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:18.530
Ask Fuko. That's who I heard it from.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.290
What, what?

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:24.790
Well, see, a boy from school died.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.210
When?

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.460
A year ago.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.880
Judas was the victim.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.420
Have you heard of Judas?

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.450
Of course not.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:38.210
And the murderer was Judas, too.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.640
The murderer was Judas, too?

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.460
Yup.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.480
Four Judas.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.120
Four Judas?

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.560
Is that someone's name?

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.930
Judas is in the Bible.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:57.570
He betrayed Christ and got him nailed to the cross.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.620
I don't get it.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.370
I was super confused, too.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.960
Why?!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.790
It's so easy...

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.260
So what class was the victim in?

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:13.260
I think ninth grade, class two.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:15.890
Mine?

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:18.020
Hey, you're right.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:22.560
Of all the places to move to.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.510
Bow.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:25.000
Goodbye.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:25.770
Goodbye.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.860
Got a sec?

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.520
Arisugawa?

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:49.830
Laters!

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:50.900
Don't let her run!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:51.460
Get her!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.420
Stop!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.050
What the hell?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.550
What did I do?

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.380
Settle down!

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.470
Let go!

00:17:58.990 --> 00:17:59.960
Hey!

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.460
Calm down!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.050
Stop kicking!

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.940
Don't struggle, Arisugawa.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.780
Let us explain.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:13.250
You've broken the barrier.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:14.440
Barrier?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:15.230
Yes!

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:16.610
What barrier?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.970
See, that desk was where we sealed Judas' soul.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:20.850
Sealed what?

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.230
See, we locked up his soul and threw away the key.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:25.940
But you broke the lock.

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.210
I didn't do anything!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.540
You did plenty!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.400
Ow!

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.630
You entered the barrier.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.240
How is that my fault?

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:35.340
This is my seat!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.620
That's human logic.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:38.010
It won't sate the anger of Judas' soul.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:39.150
So what?

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:40.610
So...

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:41.800
So!

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:45.360
Do you know what happens to people who sit here?

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.100
What?

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.270
They disappear!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:50.760
Disappear?

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.490
And go where?

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.850
To the underworld.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.160
Who are you?

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.040
I am Mutsumi Mutsu.{I think this is supposed to be something like 666}

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.200
I've been summoned from the underworld to haunt this world.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:07.370
Seat number: Friday the 13th.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:25.120
Anaphylaxis! Anaphylaxis! 
Please save the poor transfer student!{repeat}

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.330
Please save—

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.090
The Devil's messenger!

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.970
Don't touch it!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.580
Judas, go back to Hell!

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:40.270
Oh God, save Arisugawa from her curse!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.170
Here, Arisugawa.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:49.370
H!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.000
E!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:50.580
L!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.620
L!

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.870
Hell!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.360
The underworld!

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.810
We did it!

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.070
Judas is back in Hell!

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.500
Arisugawa.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:03.780
What message did you receive from the Anaphylactic God?

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.560
A cross!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.840
He did it!

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.610
God defeated the evil being!

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.630
Congratulations!

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.500
Congratulations!

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.630
Praise be to Him!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:23.400
Everyone, praise Him!

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.680
Holy crap.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:32.100
The Devil and demons actually exist in some places.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.130
I'm so glad I moved here.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.280
Maybe I'll even meet Casper!

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.590
Cut up that paper plane.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:44.900
Whoa!

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:00.020
Mommy, you're awesome!

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.360
It's a simple trick.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:06.660
Then what was that, "Let my people go!" stuff about?

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:13.720
There's a song, "Go Down Moses" that talks about Moses and the Pharaohs.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:16.180
It's a line from there.

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:20.230
Basically the chorus.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.510
God speaks to Moses, saying,

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:27.970
"Tell old Pharaoh, let my people go."

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:32.290
Oh, and Judas is Judas Iscariot.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:38.010
He was one of Jesus Christ's twelve apostles
 and a traitor who betrayed him.

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.290
What I'm saying is...

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:44.460
I don't know.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:46.200
Go google it.

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:00.140
Hey, devil girl! Want a chicken wing?

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.100
Well, too bad!

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:03.560
Man, that's good!

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:06.130
Juicy and delicious chicken wings in the morning are the best!

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:08.900
You ignoring me, bitch?

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:38.910
Who's a monster again? Huh?

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:40.410
I didn't say monster.

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:41.750
I said devil girl, duh!

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:43.980
Shut up. Same diff.

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:47.050
Where do you get off munching on chicken wings and antagonizing people?

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:48.840
You're the real devil here.

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:49.430
Bastard!

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:51.470
Ow!

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.830
Don't mess with me just cuz I'm new.

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:54.900
My traveling's made me wise.

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:57.470
Got that? Now piss off and don't bother me again.

00:22:57.470 --> 00:22:58.210
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:22:58.210 --> 00:22:59.350
Please don't hit me!

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:01.100
Who's "Judas"?

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:02.400
Spit it out.

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:03.940
Judas...

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:06.150
Judas was an older student.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:07.480
That was killed?

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:07.900
Yes!

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:09.300
Killed by who?

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:10.580
By four other Judas.

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:12.530
Who are <i>they</i>?

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:13.820
Judas' wives.

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:16.020
They were in middle school, weren't they?

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:17.950
They were the same age as us.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.720
Who has a wife at that age?

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:22.540
And four? Jesus Christ.

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:23.720
I don't understand it either!

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.460
To be honest, I don't believe in ghosts and devils.

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:27.810
Oh yeah?

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:29.760
Yet you had no problem calling me a devil girl, huh?

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:31.940
Okay, I admit that.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:35.650
But I really don't believe in such superstitious nonsense.

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:39.390
Now I think I do, though.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:42.610
I <i>saw</i> Judas' ghost.

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.150
Not.

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.510
Everyone in the class has seen it.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:49.940
Not...

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:52.170
It appeared right in the middle of class.

00:23:52.170 --> 00:23:55.090
Scared the hell out of everyone.

00:23:55.090 --> 00:23:59.950
Just flew into the room and possessed Mu.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:02.250
Mu? What?

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:03.450
Mutsumi Mutsu.

00:24:03.450 --> 00:24:06.360
You know, the girl that started that exorcism ritual.

00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:07.540
That's Mu.

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:10.350
She was possessed...

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.090
by Judas.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:24.600
My name is Judas!

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:26.680
Anaphylaxis! Anaphylaxis!

00:24:26.680 --> 00:24:28.420
Anaphylaxis!

00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:30.320
Who killed me?

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:31.930
Anaphylaxis! Anaphylaxis!

00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:33.400
Anaphylaxis!

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:34.820
Was it you?!

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:38.780
It was you, I bet!

00:24:38.780 --> 00:24:39.830
It was you!

00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:48.730
Jesus Christ.

00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:50.800
It-It's true.

00:24:51.630 --> 00:24:53.820
I was so scared I actually voided my bladder in public.

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:56.900
That made me so embarrassed I actually cried, too.

00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:59.240
They used to call me Yuya the Fierce.

00:24:59.240 --> 00:25:00.630
Chiba, the Ultimate Weapon.

00:25:00.630 --> 00:25:04.050
School Hunter Yuya. People feared my name!

00:25:04.050 --> 00:25:06.300
But after that day everyone lost respect for me.

00:25:06.300 --> 00:25:09.500
Now they call me Chiba the Pisser and Pooya.

00:25:09.500 --> 00:25:11.160
Even Diaper Boy.

00:25:12.030 --> 00:25:13.690
You've been through a lot, huh?

00:25:14.300 --> 00:25:16.990
Ever since I've been picking on girls and the weaker to make myself feel better.

00:25:16.990 --> 00:25:17.710
Well don't!

00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:19.070
Please don't hit me, it hurts!

00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:23.170
So? What happened to Mutsumi Mutsu?

00:25:24.160 --> 00:25:27.250
She was discovered in the hall bathroom,
 refusing to come out.

00:25:27.250 --> 00:25:29.490
The teachers had to drag her away.

00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:37.050
She came to school just fine the next day, but her skirt and hair were suddenly long.

00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:38.220
She was wearing a wig?

00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:40.520
She said it grew overnight.

00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:42.050
Yeah right.

00:25:42.050 --> 00:25:45.020
Anyway, she just walked this desk and chair out of nowhere

00:25:45.020 --> 00:25:47.960
and sat them down by the rear window.

00:25:47.960 --> 00:25:50.220
They remain there to this day.

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:53.570
Anaphylaxis! Anaphylaxis!

00:25:52.020 --> 00:25:56.780
She would later erect a barrier, sealing away the troubling Judas in his seat.

00:25:56.780 --> 00:25:59.260
No one can disobey Mu.

00:25:59.260 --> 00:26:04.000
Once there was a group of girls who bullied her, but now they're her slaves.

00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:07.330
This "Mu" was bullied before everything blew up?

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:09.720
She was.

00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:14.600
I participated in it as well, but that was nothing compared to the girls.

00:26:14.600 --> 00:26:16.780
But now Mu is invincible.

00:26:16.780 --> 00:26:19.840
No human can touch her if she can erect barriers.

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:22.050
That'd be like fighting a lion bare-handed.

00:26:22.050 --> 00:26:26.060
People only bully because they know their victims can't raise a finger against them.

00:26:26.450 --> 00:26:28.230
Bullying is wrong, you bastard!

00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:28.480
Ow! Stop it!

00:26:28.480 --> 00:26:29.020
No punching!

00:26:32.040 --> 00:26:33.560
On your marks.

00:26:36.560 --> 00:26:37.830
Get set.

00:26:38.540 --> 00:26:39.910
Go!

00:26:40.570 --> 00:26:42.730
A relay runner?

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:44.200
That's great!

00:26:47.100 --> 00:26:48.360
What's up?

00:26:49.200 --> 00:26:51.900
Who cares if I'm fast?

00:26:51.900 --> 00:26:54.250
I'd rather have some other skill.

00:26:54.250 --> 00:26:56.380
Oh? Like what?

00:26:56.380 --> 00:26:57.730
I dunno.

00:26:58.210 --> 00:27:00.890
Something more useful, I guess.

00:27:01.340 --> 00:27:03.940
What's wrong with being fast?

00:27:03.940 --> 00:27:05.310
You can run in the Olympics!

00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:08.180
I bet you could do it.

00:27:08.550 --> 00:27:10.690
What about you? Were you fast?

00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:13.440
Yup. So fast.

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:15.360
Did you run in the Olympics?

00:27:15.770 --> 00:27:16.320
No way.

00:27:16.640 --> 00:27:18.320
See? No way in hell.

00:27:18.320 --> 00:27:21.490
No, you see, Daddy's always been second in everything.

00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:26.210
Dessert will be served next.

00:27:26.210 --> 00:27:27.840
My, girl, your skin's so fair.

00:27:27.840 --> 00:27:29.250
You look like a porcelain doll.

00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:32.200
What should we order...

00:27:30.530 --> 00:27:32.200
Two green tea ice creams.

00:27:33.440 --> 00:27:35.020
Coming right up.

00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:42.450
Or would you rather something else?

00:27:42.450 --> 00:27:45.430
You sound like your mother.

00:27:47.190 --> 00:27:50.020
You've heard of people pushing for tenths of a second faster, right?

00:27:50.810 --> 00:27:53.330
But whatever their time, they're still fast as hell.

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:57.310
Not many people that fast in the world.

00:27:58.510 --> 00:28:02.770
It always pained me to see people like that competing.

00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:08.640
When I was a kid I pit this rhinoceros beetle against a stag beetle.

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:11.650
Those people always remind me of that.

00:28:12.350 --> 00:28:17.570
And people who think like that can't be gold-medalists.

00:28:17.570 --> 00:28:18.880
Nope.

00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:26.700
I bet that's work.

00:28:26.700 --> 00:28:28.100
Answer it.

00:28:28.100 --> 00:28:31.680
Wow, you sounded even more like your mother there.

00:28:33.980 --> 00:28:35.000
Hello?

00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:57.180
Sorry.

00:28:57.180 --> 00:28:58.560
We'll do this again.

00:28:59.990 --> 00:29:01.390
Say hi to your mother for me.

00:29:44.120 --> 00:29:45.550
Daddy!

00:29:51.800 --> 00:29:52.580
What's up?

00:29:52.580 --> 00:29:55.730
Mommy said you need to read this.

00:29:55.730 --> 00:29:57.230
Oh, thank you.

00:29:57.230 --> 00:29:59.060
What, a new volume?

00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:01.480
Ouch.

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:05.410
Wait, did you run all the way here?

00:30:05.410 --> 00:30:06.740
You really are fast!

00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:11.490
Have fun at work.

00:30:11.490 --> 00:30:13.740
And you have fun on the track team.

00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:12.620
Gold's gonna take some time.

00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:19.020
Hey, it's Ms. Ogino.

00:31:24.680 --> 00:31:27.940
Shit, it's that trash lady from the flower house.

00:31:29.210 --> 00:31:32.410
Did I raise her wrong?

00:31:32.410 --> 00:31:34.170
No, of course not.

00:31:37.620 --> 00:31:39.890
Mrs. Arai, are you okay?

00:31:40.690 --> 00:31:41.920
Forgive me.

00:31:41.920 --> 00:31:44.560
The trash lady's crying!

00:31:47.080 --> 00:31:49.240
Thank you very much.

00:31:57.940 --> 00:31:59.320
Ms. Ogino!

00:31:59.320 --> 00:32:01.020
Oh, Arisugawa.

00:32:01.020 --> 00:32:03.580
Why was that lady apologizing?

00:32:03.580 --> 00:32:04.920
Why was she crying?

00:32:04.920 --> 00:32:07.650
Well, she's been through a lot.

00:32:08.300 --> 00:32:10.400
She's my neighbor.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:11.790
Neighbor?

00:32:11.790 --> 00:32:13.690
She's the Jerry to my Tom every morning.

00:32:13.690 --> 00:32:15.160
Jerry to your Tom?

00:32:15.820 --> 00:32:18.640
She's always going on about the neighborhood dumping rules.

00:32:18.640 --> 00:32:20.450
She has a daughter in our class.

00:32:20.450 --> 00:32:22.250
Hana Arai.

00:32:22.250 --> 00:32:25.970
You remember the empty desk behind you, right?

00:32:25.970 --> 00:32:27.730
That's her seat.

00:32:28.820 --> 00:32:31.340
So that's who that is.

00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:34.570
There's this creepy girl that's always peering out the window.

00:32:34.570 --> 00:32:36.200
What's her deal?

00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:40.930
If only we knew.

00:32:42.190 --> 00:32:44.730
What was her name again?

00:32:44.730 --> 00:32:46.410
Hana Arai.

00:32:46.410 --> 00:32:47.440
See you.

00:32:52.420 --> 00:32:56.250
Go! You can do it!

00:32:56.980 --> 00:32:58.410
Keep it going!

00:33:09.540 --> 00:33:12.170
You've got it! You've got it!

00:33:17.520 --> 00:33:21.600
Hooray! Hooray!

00:33:21.600 --> 00:33:23.680
Hooray!

00:33:25.560 --> 00:33:28.280
You're amazing, girl!

00:33:28.280 --> 00:33:30.770
How did you get to be so fast?

00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:33.130
And here I thought you were being bullied out of school.

00:33:33.130 --> 00:33:35.170
Everyone loves you!

00:33:35.170 --> 00:33:36.100
When did you get here?

00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:37.430
Just now.

00:33:37.430 --> 00:33:39.210
I said you didn't have to come.

00:33:39.210 --> 00:33:40.090
Well I'm here.

00:33:40.090 --> 00:33:42.510
What're you wearing? You're totally standing out, Mommy.

00:33:42.510 --> 00:33:44.080
Oh, come on.

00:33:44.080 --> 00:33:45.930
I haven't been out in three days.

00:33:45.930 --> 00:33:47.570
I went all out.

00:33:47.570 --> 00:33:49.440
Want a drink?

00:33:49.440 --> 00:33:50.350
No thanks.

00:33:50.350 --> 00:33:51.000
Have fun.

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:53.360
Wait, what's the next event?

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:56.550
Man.

00:33:56.550 --> 00:33:58.220
I wanna go home now—

00:33:58.220 --> 00:34:00.400
What was that?

00:33:58.220 --> 00:33:59.080
Urgh.

00:34:00.400 --> 00:34:02.670
Why'd you go "urgh" just now?

00:34:02.670 --> 00:34:03.640
Huh?

00:34:03.640 --> 00:34:05.530
That was my mother. What do you want?

00:34:05.530 --> 00:34:06.790
What? Where?

00:34:06.790 --> 00:34:08.530
I know you know. Don't look away.

00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:11.840
Whoa, what the hell?

00:34:11.840 --> 00:34:13.190
She's even crazier than my mom.

00:34:13.190 --> 00:34:15.200
You saw her and got creeped out, didn't you?

00:34:15.200 --> 00:34:15.950
Nah, no way.

00:34:15.950 --> 00:34:16.640
You did.

00:34:16.640 --> 00:34:19.180
You do realize who you have to thank for your popularity, right?

00:34:19.180 --> 00:34:19.760
Me. Me!

00:34:19.760 --> 00:34:23.320
I purified you so now everyone accepts you.

00:34:23.320 --> 00:34:24.440
Basically, you owe me your life!

00:34:24.440 --> 00:34:26.860
So what do you think you're doing, looking at my mom and going "urgh"?

00:34:26.860 --> 00:34:27.970
I didn't, I swear.

00:34:27.970 --> 00:34:28.950
You did.

00:34:29.470 --> 00:34:30.930
Not that I blame you, though.

00:34:30.930 --> 00:34:33.560
What's she thinking, acting goth when she's past fifty?

00:34:33.560 --> 00:34:35.880
I told her not to come, but she never listens.

00:34:35.880 --> 00:34:40.770
They say men are from Mars and women from Venus,
 but parents are from, like, Pluto!

00:34:40.770 --> 00:34:42.860
No, seriously.

00:34:42.860 --> 00:34:45.590
I wasn't scared by your mom.

00:34:45.590 --> 00:34:46.410
Don't look.

00:34:46.410 --> 00:34:47.950
There's a lady under that tree.

00:34:47.950 --> 00:34:48.980
That's who scared me.

00:34:48.980 --> 00:34:50.210
Don't look! Don't look!

00:34:49.510 --> 00:34:51.010
How am I supposed to tell, then?

00:34:51.010 --> 00:34:52.810
Careful, then. Careful.

00:34:58.360 --> 00:35:01.540
Oh! That lady with the major nasty juju coming off her?

00:35:01.540 --> 00:35:04.390
You must be pretty sensitive to be able to spot her.

00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:07.330
Wow, no. She's my neighbor.

00:35:07.330 --> 00:35:08.380
Seriously?

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.490
That's the Haunting Mom.

00:35:11.490 --> 00:35:13.610
Huh? Haunting Mom?

00:35:13.610 --> 00:35:15.890
The girl who used to sit behind you got sucked into Hell.

00:35:15.890 --> 00:35:17.400
That's her mom.

00:35:19.510 --> 00:35:20.890
I feel for her.

00:35:20.890 --> 00:35:25.510
She still holds on to the memory of her daughter and haunts the campus.

00:35:26.470 --> 00:35:28.000
Her daughter's at home.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:29.010
Never leaves.

00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:30.420
What, you knew?

00:35:30.980 --> 00:35:33.140
I guess you are neighbors.

00:35:33.140 --> 00:35:34.150
Hey.

00:35:34.970 --> 00:35:36.560
What's this Judas business?

00:35:47.110 --> 00:35:51.220
Swear to me that you'll never tell anyone what I'm about to reveal to you.

00:35:51.220 --> 00:35:54.530
You do and I'll curse you to the end of your days.

00:35:54.530 --> 00:35:56.060
All right...

00:36:06.660 --> 00:36:09.690
Judas was a student here last year.

00:36:10.480 --> 00:36:12.550
He had four wives.

00:36:12.550 --> 00:36:15.680
But none of them knew about the others.

00:36:15.680 --> 00:36:18.580
Until one day, they found out!

00:36:18.580 --> 00:36:20.280
And he was poisoned!

00:36:20.280 --> 00:36:22.700
By something called "anaphylaxis".

00:36:22.700 --> 00:36:24.660
No one knows who poisoned him.

00:36:24.660 --> 00:36:28.550
The four wives never talked about his death.

00:36:28.550 --> 00:36:30.680
Anaphylaxis...

00:36:30.680 --> 00:36:32.720
You sure you don't mean anal laxative?

00:36:32.720 --> 00:36:34.260
But he was in middle school!

00:36:34.260 --> 00:36:35.780
How could he have had wives?

00:36:35.780 --> 00:36:36.420
Good point.

00:36:36.790 --> 00:36:38.110
No way it happened.

00:36:38.110 --> 00:36:39.740
Man, you sure are smart.

00:36:39.740 --> 00:36:42.110
Not like all the idiots in our class.

00:36:42.110 --> 00:36:44.640
Honestly, I don't believe in any of this crap.

00:36:44.640 --> 00:36:47.150
Besides, a murder just sounds so BS.

00:36:47.150 --> 00:36:50.650
If it was a murder, wouldn't like the police and reporters come?

00:36:50.650 --> 00:36:53.490
But no one showed up last year.

00:36:53.490 --> 00:36:55.280
You've heard local ghost stories before, right?

00:36:55.280 --> 00:36:57.110
It's basically like that.

00:36:57.110 --> 00:36:59.120
Some people just get off on that.

00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:00.230
Just don't bother with them.

00:37:00.230 --> 00:37:02.570
But they say you were possessed by Judas.

00:37:02.570 --> 00:37:03.880
Hell no!

00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:05.780
That was my seat first.

00:37:05.780 --> 00:37:07.130
Your seat.

00:37:07.530 --> 00:37:08.680
It sucked!

00:37:08.680 --> 00:37:10.730
No one would talk to me.

00:37:10.730 --> 00:37:13.590
People would call me Judas all the time.

00:37:13.590 --> 00:37:14.750
So what do you think I did?

00:37:14.750 --> 00:37:15.960
What?

00:37:15.960 --> 00:37:18.380
I got Judas to possess me.

00:37:18.380 --> 00:37:20.090
In front of everyone.

00:37:21.470 --> 00:37:23.110
Anaphylaxis! Anaphylaxis!

00:37:23.110 --> 00:37:25.090
Anaphylaxis!

00:37:25.480 --> 00:37:28.920
If that didn't work, I was ready to quit school.

00:37:28.920 --> 00:37:30.400
But it worked, so who cares?

00:37:30.400 --> 00:37:32.130
How'd you get possessed?

00:37:32.540 --> 00:37:33.950
It was an act.

00:37:33.950 --> 00:37:35.210
An act?

00:37:36.730 --> 00:37:39.190
So, what <i>is</i> Judas?

00:37:39.190 --> 00:37:40.060
Don't know.

00:37:40.060 --> 00:37:41.320
What? You don't?

00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:42.290
Nope.

00:37:42.290 --> 00:37:45.110
I'm a victim of Judas, just like you.

00:37:45.110 --> 00:37:47.960
I've got no clue who Judas or his four wives are.

00:37:49.070 --> 00:37:54.000
In fact, it was last year's ninth graders that started this.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:55.950
It might be just a rumor.

00:37:55.950 --> 00:37:57.540
Or it might not!

00:37:57.540 --> 00:38:01.230
Perhaps there really was an incident that birthed this tale.

00:38:01.230 --> 00:38:04.220
It's all shrouded in mystery now, though.

00:38:08.300 --> 00:38:09.610
Hana Arai.

00:38:11.250 --> 00:38:12.390
Her?

00:38:12.800 --> 00:38:15.440
She might know something.

00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:19.440
She's the only eyewitness remaining from last year's class.

00:38:23.310 --> 00:38:27.950
Never went to school after, so she couldn't graduate.

00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:32.680
Hey, was that teacher around?

00:38:33.330 --> 00:38:34.390
Who?

00:38:34.390 --> 00:38:36.760
You know! From your first day at school.

00:38:36.760 --> 00:38:39.330
With the snails!

00:38:39.870 --> 00:38:42.210
Actually, I haven't seen him since.

00:38:47.780 --> 00:38:50.390
Oh, that must be the person who used to live here.

00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:53.720
Yuda?

00:39:15.920 --> 00:39:18.750
This is Yuda's room!

00:39:19.170 --> 00:39:21.960
Man, I'm beat.

00:39:29.540 --> 00:39:30.650
Mommy, we need to move.

00:39:30.650 --> 00:39:31.550
Let's move!

00:39:31.550 --> 00:39:33.050
I can't live here!

00:39:33.050 --> 00:39:35.680
I can't, can't, can't!

00:39:34.300 --> 00:39:37.600
Tetsuko?

00:39:35.680 --> 00:39:37.600
I can't!

00:39:38.740 --> 00:39:40.650
I don't want to live in the sticks!

00:39:39.630 --> 00:39:41.940
You're hurting me!

00:39:40.650 --> 00:39:42.440
The anaphylaxis crap makes no sense!

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:44.530
Let go, would you?

00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:44.530
This is all because you're splitting up with Daddy!

00:39:44.530 --> 00:39:47.860
You just had to write it all down in your stupid book, and now we're cursed!

00:39:49.850 --> 00:39:52.780
What happened? Tell me.

00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:57.800
The person who used to live here died.

00:39:58.880 --> 00:40:00.770
What are you going on about?

00:40:00.770 --> 00:40:02.310
Talk to me, here.

00:40:02.870 --> 00:40:04.810
Come, Tetsuko. Talk!

00:40:08.090 --> 00:40:09.640
Forget it.

00:40:09.640 --> 00:40:10.860
Tell me!

00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:14.580
I swear I won't write about it, so tell me.

00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:16.640
That was close.

00:40:16.640 --> 00:40:17.880
What am I doing?

00:40:18.400 --> 00:40:19.960
What do you mean, close?

00:40:42.410 --> 00:40:43.290
Huh?

00:40:46.860 --> 00:40:49.050
Hello?

00:40:55.640 --> 00:40:57.580
Hello?

00:40:57.580 --> 00:40:59.790
Um...

00:40:59.790 --> 00:41:01.930
Hana Arai?

00:41:03.430 --> 00:41:05.770
Don't mind if I do.

00:41:11.480 --> 00:41:14.610
Hana?{Warriors~}

00:41:15.080 --> 00:41:17.320
Come out to play...

00:41:55.970 --> 00:41:58.020
You okay?

00:42:00.680 --> 00:42:03.140
I'm done for. Paralyzed.{"No response. It looks like a corpse." for extra meme points}

00:42:06.900 --> 00:42:09.220
What're you doing in my house?

00:42:09.220 --> 00:42:10.920
That's breaking and entering.

00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:14.360
I won't call the cops, so get out.

00:42:14.360 --> 00:42:17.310
Sorry. Gimme time to recover my senses.

00:42:17.310 --> 00:42:18.600
Like a minute.

00:42:19.080 --> 00:42:21.090
Fine. A minute.

00:42:21.090 --> 00:42:22.730
Thanks.

00:42:22.730 --> 00:42:24.950
You dropped all your papers.

00:42:25.810 --> 00:42:27.450
These are tests.

00:42:27.450 --> 00:42:28.560
What're these for?

00:42:28.560 --> 00:42:29.850
I'm cleaning up your mess.

00:42:38.990 --> 00:42:42.580
You know Kotaro Yuda?

00:42:43.030 --> 00:42:44.410
I do.

00:42:44.410 --> 00:42:46.910
He used to live in that house of yours.

00:42:47.380 --> 00:42:49.900
You were in the same class, weren't you?

00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:50.940
I was.

00:42:50.940 --> 00:42:52.560
Was he killed?

00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:54.500
I don't know.

00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:56.580
What about his four wives?

00:42:59.010 --> 00:43:00.560
What else do you know?

00:43:00.560 --> 00:43:01.500
Huh?

00:43:02.680 --> 00:43:04.220
Well...

00:43:05.100 --> 00:43:07.740
The story goes that this Yuda guy had four wives.

00:43:07.740 --> 00:43:11.440
But one day they realized he was stepping out so one of them killed him.

00:43:11.440 --> 00:43:12.490
With poison, apparently.

00:43:12.490 --> 00:43:13.650
Poison?

00:43:13.650 --> 00:43:15.740
Something called "anaphylaxis".

00:43:15.740 --> 00:43:16.860
Heard of it?

00:43:18.900 --> 00:43:20.010
No.

00:43:21.970 --> 00:43:24.930
All I know is Yuda transferred out.

00:43:24.930 --> 00:43:26.280
Nothing else.

00:43:26.800 --> 00:43:28.330
Transferred?

00:43:28.330 --> 00:43:29.480
He wasn't killed?

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:31.170
I have no idea.

00:43:33.240 --> 00:43:35.590
What about the four Yudas? The four wives.

00:43:35.590 --> 00:43:36.920
Never heard of them.

00:43:38.020 --> 00:43:40.840
Man, he wasn't murdered?

00:43:40.840 --> 00:43:42.590
I told you, I don't know.

00:43:42.590 --> 00:43:45.090
Go play detective and find out if he's alive, since you're so hot on it.

00:43:45.090 --> 00:43:46.560
Maybe he <i>was</i> murdered!

00:43:46.560 --> 00:43:48.980
Whatever. He transferred, end of story.

00:43:48.980 --> 00:43:50.970
What if he actually was murdered?

00:43:50.970 --> 00:43:53.620
Can you really sleep in his bed knowing that?

00:43:53.620 --> 00:43:56.700
That's why I'm trying to convince myself he just transferred!

00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:58.530
Fine.

00:43:58.530 --> 00:44:00.740
I'll help you, so start detectiving.

00:44:01.210 --> 00:44:02.740
Detectiving how?

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:05.450
We have to figure out his current address first.

00:44:06.170 --> 00:44:07.200
How?

00:44:07.200 --> 00:44:09.270
Figure that out yourself.

00:44:09.270 --> 00:44:12.280
You said you'd help me!

00:44:15.630 --> 00:44:18.920
Yuda's dad worked for some company called Cobalt.

00:44:19.540 --> 00:44:22.640
Oh, I get it. We can just ask his dad.

00:44:22.640 --> 00:44:24.050
Ask him what?

00:44:24.050 --> 00:44:27.760
Like, uh, "Is Yuda alive?"

00:44:27.760 --> 00:44:30.520
You're going to scare him if you ask his dad that!

00:44:30.520 --> 00:44:34.360
If he is dead, you might get mistaken for the murderer.

00:44:36.810 --> 00:44:37.830
Listen.

00:44:37.830 --> 00:44:39.820
First, you pay a visit to Cobalt.

00:44:39.820 --> 00:44:43.020
Then you ask the receptionist if there's a Mr. Teruo Yuda.

00:44:43.020 --> 00:44:45.100
That's Yuda's dad's name.

00:44:45.100 --> 00:44:47.530
You'll probably be asked who you are.

00:44:47.530 --> 00:44:50.580
So you answer, "Kotaro Yuda."

00:44:50.580 --> 00:44:55.500
There's a cafe on the first floor called Sorun.
 Tell him to meet you there.

00:44:55.500 --> 00:44:57.680
The guy'll have to show.

00:44:57.680 --> 00:45:01.420
Then you can judge from his expression
 if Yuda is alive or not.

00:45:01.950 --> 00:45:03.300
Know how?

00:45:03.860 --> 00:45:09.930
If he's alive, the dad will look around the cafe with an irritated expression.

00:45:09.930 --> 00:45:15.650
But if he's dead, he'll probably show up shocked beyond belief.

00:45:15.650 --> 00:45:18.680
After all, he was just told his son's waiting for him in a cafe.

00:45:18.680 --> 00:45:20.100
He'd be totally panicked.

00:45:20.100 --> 00:45:23.450
The definition of looking like you've seen a ghost.

00:45:23.450 --> 00:45:24.150
Got it?

00:45:27.280 --> 00:45:28.910
Not really.

00:45:32.540 --> 00:45:34.080
I'll write you instructions.

00:45:36.530 --> 00:45:40.980
Oh, and when you go, make sure to wear boy clothes.

00:45:40.980 --> 00:45:44.490
If you call yourself Kotaro and show up looking like a girl, they'll know you're a fake.

00:45:48.770 --> 00:45:51.370
Did you just think of that?

00:45:51.370 --> 00:45:52.450
Yeah.

00:45:52.450 --> 00:45:53.680
Why?

00:45:53.680 --> 00:45:54.930
That's crazy fast.

00:45:54.930 --> 00:45:56.350
It's just normal.

00:45:57.650 --> 00:45:59.570
So I'm supposed to go alone?

00:45:59.570 --> 00:46:01.620
Yeah. You'll be fine.

00:46:01.620 --> 00:46:03.770
Come with me!

00:46:03.770 --> 00:46:05.400
I can't.

00:46:05.400 --> 00:46:07.540
His dad knows me.

00:46:07.540 --> 00:46:09.250
Go by yourself.

00:46:10.770 --> 00:46:12.340
I'm not going.

00:46:14.530 --> 00:46:15.710
Why?

00:46:16.360 --> 00:46:19.610
Cuz I'm not that curious.

00:46:19.610 --> 00:46:20.970
Sorry.

00:46:20.970 --> 00:46:22.750
I know you put all that thought into it.

00:46:23.750 --> 00:46:25.260
You better go!

00:46:28.030 --> 00:46:30.800
Go! Please!

00:46:30.800 --> 00:46:32.100
Why?

00:46:32.100 --> 00:46:34.100
This is a person's life on the line!

00:46:34.100 --> 00:46:35.940
Can you really just sit there if someone might be dead?

00:46:35.940 --> 00:46:38.940
What's with you? Do you not care about human life at all?

00:46:38.940 --> 00:46:40.350
Wow, what a bitch!

00:46:40.760 --> 00:46:42.280
You'll curse yourself forever!

00:46:42.280 --> 00:46:45.280
You'll wish you'd gone and learned the truth!

00:46:46.620 --> 00:46:48.860
F-Fine!

00:46:48.860 --> 00:46:51.310
All right, that's a minute.

00:46:52.110 --> 00:46:53.210
Get out.

00:46:56.050 --> 00:46:58.160
Here. I wrote everything out.

00:46:58.160 --> 00:47:01.730
My phone number, too. If something happens, call.

00:47:02.500 --> 00:47:03.790
You better go.

00:47:05.130 --> 00:47:06.890
Oh, what's your name?

00:47:06.890 --> 00:47:08.220
Tetsuko Kuro—

00:47:08.730 --> 00:47:09.860
I mean, Tetsuko Arisugawa.

00:47:09.860 --> 00:47:12.220
Tetsuko Arisugawa. I'm—

00:47:12.220 --> 00:47:13.520
Hana Arai.

00:47:14.860 --> 00:47:16.460
Smartass.

00:47:19.510 --> 00:47:21.970
You were the one asking for names.

00:47:41.540 --> 00:47:42.930
Whoa, what's that?

00:47:42.930 --> 00:47:44.140
A balloon?

00:47:45.190 --> 00:47:46.800
Hello?

00:47:46.800 --> 00:47:49.050
Hey! What're you doing?

00:47:49.050 --> 00:47:50.850
It's a hot-air balloon!

00:47:50.850 --> 00:47:52.460
Crazy close.

00:47:52.460 --> 00:47:54.180
Don't you mean blimp?

00:47:54.180 --> 00:47:55.330
What?

00:47:55.330 --> 00:47:56.840
That's not a hot-air balloon?

00:47:57.530 --> 00:47:59.050
How can you tell?

00:47:59.050 --> 00:48:00.540
Are you spying on me?

00:48:00.540 --> 00:48:02.240
I can tell without seeing it.

00:48:02.240 --> 00:48:04.630
Hot-air balloons don't float over cities.

00:48:04.630 --> 00:48:08.210
And who cares about that? Did you find Cobalt?

00:48:08.210 --> 00:48:09.870
Holy cow.

00:48:09.870 --> 00:48:11.810
Hey!

00:48:12.840 --> 00:48:14.720
Cobalt... Cobalt...{repeat}

00:48:14.720 --> 00:48:18.430
Cobalt... Cobalt... Cobalt...

00:48:18.430 --> 00:48:22.000
Cobalt... Cobalt...

00:48:25.600 --> 00:48:27.620
Maybe this one?

00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:37.890
I'm so sorry for not telling you sooner.

00:48:38.270 --> 00:48:39.490
Here's my card.

00:48:39.490 --> 00:48:41.010
See the receptionist?

00:48:41.010 --> 00:48:42.290
Yup.

00:48:42.290 --> 00:48:44.980
Now ask if there's a Teruo Yuda in.

00:48:44.980 --> 00:48:47.050
Not Kotaro. First you say Teruo.

00:48:47.050 --> 00:48:48.450
You're Kotaro, remember.

00:48:48.450 --> 00:48:49.490
Okay.

00:48:56.300 --> 00:48:59.520
Excuse me, is this Cobalt?

00:48:59.520 --> 00:49:02.060
Yes, it is.

00:49:02.060 --> 00:49:04.690
Is there someone named Teruo Yuda in?

00:49:04.690 --> 00:49:06.180
Teruo Yuda.

00:49:07.600 --> 00:49:10.470
Teruo Yuda, from the Third Planning Office?

00:49:10.470 --> 00:49:12.090
Yes, that's the one.

00:49:12.540 --> 00:49:14.280
May I ask your name?

00:49:14.280 --> 00:49:15.060
Huh?

00:49:15.060 --> 00:49:16.720
Your name, please.

00:49:17.080 --> 00:49:19.250
Uh, Kuro—

00:49:19.250 --> 00:49:20.310
I mean, Arisugawa.

00:49:20.310 --> 00:49:21.690
Tetsuko Arisugawa.

00:49:21.690 --> 00:49:24.610
Ms. Arisugawa, then. Just a moment.

00:49:27.240 --> 00:49:29.100
I have a visitor for Mr. Yuda.

00:49:29.100 --> 00:49:31.130
Yes, she's waiting in the first floor lobby.

00:49:31.130 --> 00:49:32.190
Should he meet you here?

00:49:32.720 --> 00:49:35.490
Oh, I'll be waiting in the cafe.

00:49:35.490 --> 00:49:37.260
Name of Sorun.

00:49:36.810 --> 00:49:38.880
Alice!

00:49:37.260 --> 00:49:39.640
She'll be waiting at Sorun Cafe.

00:49:38.880 --> 00:49:39.640
Alice!

00:49:39.640 --> 00:49:40.280
Can you hear me?

00:49:40.280 --> 00:49:42.490
Earth to Alice!

00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:43.920
Hello?

00:49:43.920 --> 00:49:45.510
What did you just say?

00:49:45.510 --> 00:49:47.580
I heard Tetsuko Arisugawa.

00:49:47.580 --> 00:49:49.010
Uh, what?

00:49:49.010 --> 00:49:50.560
Your name!

00:49:50.560 --> 00:49:52.600
Did you give them Kotaro Yuda as your name?

00:49:53.760 --> 00:49:56.970
Yes. A Ms. Tetsuko Arisugawa.

00:49:58.090 --> 00:50:00.480
Sorry. I screwed up.

00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:01.970
Useless!

00:50:03.040 --> 00:50:07.190
Yuda's in a meeting with a client right now.

00:50:07.190 --> 00:50:08.130
Yes.

00:50:08.850 --> 00:50:12.620
Everyone's out right now. It's just me.

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:14.930
What does she want?

00:50:15.390 --> 00:50:19.250
Actually, never mind. I'll be down soon.

00:50:19.250 --> 00:50:21.870
Nothing else to do.

00:50:31.260 --> 00:50:31.820
Welcome!

00:50:31.820 --> 00:50:33.070
Glass of orange juice.

00:50:33.070 --> 00:50:34.460
Coming right up.

00:50:39.700 --> 00:50:40.730
Hello?

00:50:40.730 --> 00:50:42.540
Everything's ruined!

00:50:42.540 --> 00:50:44.620
All our plans, down the tubes!

00:50:44.620 --> 00:50:45.770
Can I go home now?

00:50:45.770 --> 00:50:47.930
What're you talking about? Of course not!

00:50:47.930 --> 00:50:49.470
Why?

00:50:49.470 --> 00:50:51.380
I'm going back to the drawing board.

00:50:51.380 --> 00:50:52.880
Gimme a minute.

00:50:52.880 --> 00:50:54.920
I'll just wait in the cafe, then.

00:50:54.920 --> 00:50:57.280
That's not necessary. Actually, that's bad.

00:50:57.280 --> 00:50:59.280
Hide outside and watch the building entrance.

00:50:59.280 --> 00:51:02.940
If you see a man looking around the cafe, that's Mr. Yuda.

00:51:02.940 --> 00:51:04.740
I'm already in the cafe.

00:51:04.740 --> 00:51:05.480
What?

00:51:05.480 --> 00:51:06.890
What's wrong with you?

00:51:06.890 --> 00:51:08.660
Get out, now!

00:51:08.660 --> 00:51:10.840
I ordered orange juice.

00:51:10.840 --> 00:51:14.410
Who cares? Just go!

00:51:15.520 --> 00:51:19.160
Excuse me. Are you Ms. Arisugawa?

00:51:21.110 --> 00:51:23.210
Uh, no.

00:51:24.900 --> 00:51:27.250
Hmm. A girl in a hat.

00:51:28.680 --> 00:51:29.690
Hat...

00:51:29.690 --> 00:51:30.950
What?

00:51:30.950 --> 00:51:31.850
What do you mean, no?

00:51:33.120 --> 00:51:34.740
Ms. Arisugawa?

00:51:34.740 --> 00:51:35.540
No, sorry.

00:51:35.540 --> 00:51:38.650
Yes, of course. Pardon me.

00:51:40.610 --> 00:51:43.370
Girl in a hat...{repeat}

00:51:43.760 --> 00:51:46.400
Girl in a hat...

00:51:50.830 --> 00:51:52.420
That was close.

00:51:52.420 --> 00:51:53.880
What, what? What happened?

00:51:54.260 --> 00:51:55.830
Mr. Yuda just showed up.

00:51:55.830 --> 00:51:57.540
What? What did he want?

00:51:58.030 --> 00:52:00.430
He asked if I was Arisugawa, and I said no.

00:52:00.430 --> 00:52:02.620
He's seen your face now!

00:52:02.620 --> 00:52:03.770
Sorry.

00:52:04.370 --> 00:52:07.390
He's more like Grandpa Yuda, not Mr. Yuda, though.

00:52:07.390 --> 00:52:09.160
He's an old fart.

00:52:09.160 --> 00:52:10.860
Old? Really?

00:52:10.860 --> 00:52:13.980
Thank you for waiting. Here's your orange juice.

00:52:13.980 --> 00:52:14.770
Thanks.

00:52:14.770 --> 00:52:16.360
Enjoy your drink.

00:52:17.210 --> 00:52:19.380
Just get out of that cafe.

00:52:19.380 --> 00:52:21.000
Fine, just gimme a sec.

00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:22.610
This is no time to be drinking juice.

00:52:24.200 --> 00:52:26.410
Crap! He's back!

00:52:29.790 --> 00:52:30.710
Welcome.

00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:32.080
One hot coffee.

00:52:32.080 --> 00:52:33.340
Coming right up.

00:52:33.340 --> 00:52:35.700
What happened? What happened?

00:52:35.700 --> 00:52:37.000
Miss, please put away your phone.

00:52:42.580 --> 00:52:43.630
You dropped this.

00:52:50.940 --> 00:52:53.290
The plan was perfect, too.

00:52:53.290 --> 00:52:56.080
Now your only choice is to tail him.

00:52:57.210 --> 00:52:59.860
Tail him? For how long?

00:52:59.860 --> 00:53:01.500
To his house.

00:53:01.500 --> 00:53:03.030
His <i>house</i>?

00:53:03.640 --> 00:53:05.740
Everyone goes home after work, right?

00:53:06.160 --> 00:53:08.710
Tail him and you'll find Yuda's house.

00:53:08.710 --> 00:53:11.080
If he's alive, he'll be there.

00:53:11.580 --> 00:53:12.970
This is now a war of attrition.

00:53:14.290 --> 00:53:15.560
I wanna go home.

00:53:15.560 --> 00:53:16.690
No!

00:53:44.840 --> 00:53:46.770
That's not Mr. Yuda.

00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:49.140
What's she doing?

00:53:50.950 --> 00:53:51.910
Crap!

00:53:51.910 --> 00:53:52.700
No power!

00:53:55.870 --> 00:53:57.490
Hey, taxi!

00:54:19.010 --> 00:54:20.770
Follow that taxi!

00:54:43.030 --> 00:54:45.210
Um, this is far enough.

00:54:45.210 --> 00:54:47.340
Huh? They haven't stopped.

00:54:47.340 --> 00:54:48.630
Yes, this is fine.

00:55:02.380 --> 00:55:04.110
I'm kinda short.

00:55:04.110 --> 00:55:05.610
No money?

00:55:06.510 --> 00:55:07.860
Just short.

00:55:07.860 --> 00:55:10.440
That's why you called off the chase?

00:55:10.950 --> 00:55:12.410
Who is that?

00:55:12.410 --> 00:55:13.810
How do you know each other?

00:55:14.430 --> 00:55:16.920
Well, uh...

00:55:18.930 --> 00:55:19.920
He's my dad!

00:55:20.990 --> 00:55:23.500
He left and never came back!

00:55:23.500 --> 00:55:27.070
If I don't catch him, I'll never see him again...

00:55:29.580 --> 00:55:30.810
All right.

00:55:54.100 --> 00:55:55.720
Wait right here.

00:55:56.600 --> 00:55:57.890
Uh, okay.

00:56:02.530 --> 00:56:03.740
What's he doing?

00:56:03.740 --> 00:56:04.260
Excuse me.

00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:05.160
Yes?

00:56:07.060 --> 00:56:09.180
Uh, what?

00:56:12.130 --> 00:56:14.630
I picker her up in Osamu.

00:56:13.610 --> 00:56:14.630
What?

00:56:16.060 --> 00:56:18.590
She wanted me to follow your taxi.

00:56:18.590 --> 00:56:22.680
But she realized she had no money so she tried to get out halfway.

00:56:22.680 --> 00:56:25.500
I took it upon myself to bring her here.

00:56:26.040 --> 00:56:28.990
Maybe this is none of my business, but...

00:56:29.660 --> 00:56:30.620
Oh, right.

00:56:30.620 --> 00:56:33.280
No, I'm not talking about that.

00:56:34.300 --> 00:56:37.580
Please see her.

00:56:37.580 --> 00:56:39.580
Uh, <i>what</i>?

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:47.920
No charge.

00:56:47.920 --> 00:56:50.250
Good luck!

00:57:06.280 --> 00:57:08.540
Who are you?

00:57:08.540 --> 00:57:10.280
I'm sorry.

00:57:10.280 --> 00:57:13.740
I didn't have enough money, so I kinda lied.

00:57:13.740 --> 00:57:16.240
I said you were my father.

00:57:16.240 --> 00:57:19.640
So that's why he was pleading with me.

00:57:19.640 --> 00:57:21.060
I'm sorry.

00:57:22.680 --> 00:57:24.700
Lying's wrong, you know.

00:57:25.620 --> 00:57:27.890
But I guess you know that.

00:57:29.250 --> 00:57:31.540
Goodbye.

00:57:50.310 --> 00:57:51.840
There you are!

00:57:51.840 --> 00:57:52.940
Where are you right now?

00:57:53.330 --> 00:57:54.510
Oh, hello?

00:57:54.510 --> 00:57:57.800
I'm in a hospital waiting room.

00:57:57.800 --> 00:58:00.320
Please put away your phone.

00:58:02.440 --> 00:58:03.310
Huh?

00:58:03.310 --> 00:58:04.540
Hello?

00:58:06.250 --> 00:58:07.960
Hana!

00:58:10.620 --> 00:58:11.670
Mr. Yuda!

00:58:18.900 --> 00:58:21.980
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:58:33.360 --> 00:58:34.690
That'll be 1400 yen.

00:58:34.690 --> 00:58:36.370
Okay.

00:58:44.110 --> 00:58:45.080
Shit!

00:58:45.080 --> 00:58:45.830
What?

00:58:47.300 --> 00:58:49.690
Do you want something from me?

00:58:53.640 --> 00:58:54.890
Uh...

00:58:57.280 --> 00:58:59.040
Oh, I get it!

00:58:59.040 --> 00:59:01.260
No money to get home, huh?

00:59:01.260 --> 00:59:03.640
Where do you want to be dropped off?

00:59:03.640 --> 00:59:05.400
Where's your house?

00:59:12.160 --> 00:59:13.600
Please stop.

00:59:14.960 --> 00:59:16.360
What's the matter?

00:59:16.360 --> 00:59:17.530
Uh, nothing.

00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:26.180
Order whatever you like.

00:59:26.770 --> 00:59:29.440
Cheesecake and strawberry juice, please.

00:59:30.040 --> 00:59:32.810
I'll have...

00:59:33.220 --> 00:59:34.720
I'll...

00:59:34.720 --> 00:59:36.390
I...

00:59:38.050 --> 00:59:39.380
I'm fine.

00:59:41.190 --> 00:59:44.050
Why were you at the hospital?

00:59:44.050 --> 00:59:45.080
Visiting someone?

00:59:45.080 --> 00:59:48.170
I, uh, felt a little sick.

00:59:49.940 --> 00:59:51.900
How old are you?

00:59:51.900 --> 00:59:53.030
Huh?

00:59:53.480 --> 00:59:55.130
Uh, fourteen.

00:59:55.650 --> 00:59:57.860
Fourteen.

00:59:57.860 --> 01:00:00.530
Only fourteen years since you were born, huh?

01:00:01.680 --> 01:00:05.660
Such nice skin, too. Lovely.

01:00:06.100 --> 01:00:07.410
Perv.

01:00:07.410 --> 01:00:09.620
I don't mean it like that.

01:00:10.290 --> 01:00:14.240
When you get older, wrinkles and liver spots take you over.

01:00:14.240 --> 01:00:16.380
Your face is just a mess.

01:00:18.920 --> 01:00:22.240
You know, I was pretty handsome when I was younger.

01:00:22.980 --> 01:00:25.800
I still got it over here.

01:00:27.930 --> 01:00:31.650
Wow, mister! That one part of you is super young!

01:00:32.210 --> 01:00:33.900
Ew! What's that?

01:00:33.900 --> 01:00:35.420
You've got one long hair!

01:00:35.420 --> 01:00:36.440
Ewww!

01:00:36.440 --> 01:00:39.620
Stop saying that.

01:00:38.130 --> 01:00:39.980
Ew!

01:00:40.360 --> 01:00:43.180
I just recently spotted it.

01:00:45.080 --> 01:00:49.850
My body's checking me into the old folks club whether I like it or not.

01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:53.820
But this one spot is smooth as a newborn's.

01:00:54.670 --> 01:00:59.010
It made me check myself again.

01:00:59.570 --> 01:01:03.860
I'm still young in a few places, surprisingly!

01:01:04.650 --> 01:01:07.720
Mostly out-of-the-way ones.

01:01:08.560 --> 01:01:11.020
But they're smooth as a newborn's.

01:01:14.600 --> 01:01:19.570
The human body is a strange thing.

01:01:21.010 --> 01:01:22.930
Oh, excuse me. Bathroom break.

01:01:34.450 --> 01:01:36.750
Hello? Where are you now?

01:01:36.750 --> 01:01:39.210
I've secured Mr. Yuda!

01:01:39.210 --> 01:01:40.340
You've got the wrong guy.

01:01:40.960 --> 01:01:42.420
I'm tailing Mr. Yuda right now.

01:01:42.880 --> 01:01:44.870
The wrong guy? Then who's this?

01:01:44.870 --> 01:01:46.220
I dunno.

01:01:46.220 --> 01:01:47.740
Where are you?

01:01:47.740 --> 01:01:50.780
Some shop. He's paying for me.

01:01:50.780 --> 01:01:51.820
What the hell?

01:01:52.870 --> 01:01:54.270
You sure he's not a kidnapper?

01:01:54.270 --> 01:01:56.880
What? No way.

01:01:57.970 --> 01:01:59.840
So what do I do now?

01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:01.170
Where are you?

01:02:01.730 --> 01:02:04.030
The car took all these turns. I have no idea.

01:02:04.030 --> 01:02:07.450
Turns? He's totally a kidnapper!

01:02:08.500 --> 01:02:10.030
What?!

01:02:10.480 --> 01:02:11.080
What do I do?

01:02:12.100 --> 01:02:13.580
Just get out of there.

01:02:13.580 --> 01:02:17.240
I'll follow the real Mr. Yuda, so you focus on getting home.

01:02:17.240 --> 01:02:18.860
That's so mean!

01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:21.380
You use me all day and now you're leaving me out to dry?

01:02:22.150 --> 01:02:24.280
Fine, look for the closest station.

01:02:24.280 --> 01:02:25.880
There must be one around.

01:02:25.880 --> 01:02:27.020
A station? Okay.

01:02:27.020 --> 01:02:28.120
I'll look.

01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:29.780
Hello?

01:02:29.780 --> 01:02:30.550
The train's leaving.

01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:32.640
When you get to the station, call me.

01:02:33.030 --> 01:02:34.500
Hello?

01:02:36.390 --> 01:02:40.530
Please do not try to board a moving train.

01:02:40.530 --> 01:02:43.570
Please do not try to board a moving train.

01:02:56.480 --> 01:02:58.940
Oh. Bathroom break for you, too?

01:02:59.960 --> 01:03:01.580
Did they take our orders?

01:03:01.580 --> 01:03:03.090
No, not yet.

01:03:03.480 --> 01:03:05.760
They're holding a party here, apparently.

01:03:06.320 --> 01:03:08.300
Let's go somewhere else.

01:03:08.300 --> 01:03:09.490
Okay.

01:03:18.930 --> 01:03:21.940
Happy birthday to you!

01:03:22.580 --> 01:03:25.170
Don't see any shops.

01:03:25.170 --> 01:03:27.880
Oh, don't need to use the bathroom anymore?

01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:29.280
I'm okay.

01:03:29.280 --> 01:03:32.560
Um, I need to go home.

01:03:32.560 --> 01:03:34.140
I see.

01:03:34.140 --> 01:03:36.160
Where's the closest station?

01:03:36.160 --> 01:03:38.000
Very far.

01:03:38.460 --> 01:03:40.650
Where's your house again?

01:03:41.240 --> 01:03:42.810
In Fujiko.

01:03:42.810 --> 01:03:46.280
I see. That's on the way, then.

01:03:46.280 --> 01:03:47.180
I can drop you.

01:03:47.180 --> 01:03:48.440
But...

01:03:51.930 --> 01:03:54.440
No taxis, huh?

01:03:54.440 --> 01:03:55.460
No.

01:03:55.460 --> 01:03:57.740
Let's walk that way.

01:03:57.740 --> 01:03:59.020
Okay.

01:04:29.070 --> 01:04:30.890
Are you okay?

01:04:32.390 --> 01:04:33.250
Sorry...

01:04:33.250 --> 01:04:34.270
Sorry.

01:04:35.300 --> 01:04:36.950
Are you sick, mister?

01:04:37.560 --> 01:04:39.320
I'm getting better.

01:04:40.460 --> 01:04:43.400
I had surgery last month.

01:04:43.400 --> 01:04:45.380
Yeah, I'm fine.

01:04:48.420 --> 01:04:51.650
I just need to rest a little.

01:05:00.660 --> 01:05:01.760
Better?

01:05:05.220 --> 01:05:07.770
That's nice.

01:05:08.450 --> 01:05:10.350
I'm in heaven.

01:05:13.050 --> 01:05:14.610
That's enough.

01:05:15.010 --> 01:05:16.280
Thank you.

01:05:17.660 --> 01:05:18.930
Swings!

01:05:21.930 --> 01:05:23.090
Up we go.

01:05:31.420 --> 01:05:34.270
I used to do this all the time!

01:05:39.930 --> 01:05:41.140
Whew.

01:05:49.240 --> 01:05:51.070
How long's it been?

01:05:51.070 --> 01:05:52.880
Two years, maybe?

01:05:53.840 --> 01:05:55.600
What about you, mister?

01:05:57.320 --> 01:05:59.000
Forty years.

01:05:59.600 --> 01:06:02.020
Forty? That's crazy.

01:06:02.020 --> 01:06:04.650
Back when my daughter was in elementary school.

01:06:04.650 --> 01:06:06.930
Forty years, huh?

01:06:07.830 --> 01:06:09.810
How time flies.

01:06:09.810 --> 01:06:12.820
That's a long time! Super long!

01:06:14.100 --> 01:06:17.610
Yes, perhaps it is.

01:06:25.960 --> 01:06:27.640
Hey, the station!

01:06:27.640 --> 01:06:30.200
I guess we ended up walking there anyway.

01:06:51.340 --> 01:06:52.820
Thank you!

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:54.200
Bye.

01:07:04.440 --> 01:07:05.370
Hello?

01:07:05.370 --> 01:07:07.370
Oh! How'd it go?

01:07:07.370 --> 01:07:10.300
I found the station and bid the weird old man farewell.

01:07:10.300 --> 01:07:11.130
What?

01:07:11.130 --> 01:07:13.350
You were with him the whole time?

01:07:13.350 --> 01:07:15.200
He wasn't a bad guy.

01:07:15.200 --> 01:07:16.820
Whatever. I'm off the train.

01:07:16.820 --> 01:07:18.100
Can you get to Hinoka Station?

01:07:18.100 --> 01:07:19.450
Take the Reimei Line.

01:07:19.450 --> 01:07:20.720
I'll be waiting.

01:07:20.720 --> 01:07:21.570
What?

01:07:21.570 --> 01:07:23.610
Can't I go home?

01:07:23.610 --> 01:07:25.740
The situation changes every minute.

01:07:25.740 --> 01:07:27.500
Just hurry.

01:07:38.070 --> 01:07:41.460
The doors will be closing.

01:07:39.090 --> 01:07:40.530
Wait, wait!

01:07:41.460 --> 01:07:42.740
Please be careful.

01:07:46.760 --> 01:07:48.000
Took you long enough.

01:07:48.580 --> 01:07:50.230
Good. I need to borrow this.

01:07:50.230 --> 01:07:53.190
The Yudas know me.

01:07:53.920 --> 01:07:55.460
H-Hey, wait! Where are you going?

01:07:55.460 --> 01:07:57.080
Just come.

01:07:58.960 --> 01:08:00.690
Where are we going?

01:08:01.410 --> 01:08:02.430
Hey!

01:08:03.040 --> 01:08:04.740
Hey!

01:08:05.360 --> 01:08:06.800
Hey-hey!

01:08:07.630 --> 01:08:09.890
How far are we going?

01:08:10.780 --> 01:08:12.940
Say something!

01:08:13.560 --> 01:08:14.540
Hey!

01:08:23.970 --> 01:08:25.070
There's Yuda's house.

01:08:29.920 --> 01:08:30.690
Which one?

01:08:30.690 --> 01:08:31.960
Dunno.

01:08:31.960 --> 01:08:34.540
There's security so I couldn't get in.

01:08:34.540 --> 01:08:36.490
I wonder if this kid's alive.

01:08:36.490 --> 01:08:38.520
We can't leave until we find out.

01:08:38.520 --> 01:08:39.690
How do we do that?

01:08:40.260 --> 01:08:42.700
He should be coming home soon.

01:08:42.700 --> 01:08:44.840
Wouldn't he already be home?

01:08:44.840 --> 01:08:47.570
He wasn't a goody two-shoes.

01:08:47.570 --> 01:08:51.040
Usually stayed out, ate something, 
and came home around nine or ten.

01:08:51.040 --> 01:08:52.650
You sure know him well.

01:08:52.650 --> 01:08:54.800
We were friends for a long time.

01:08:54.800 --> 01:08:58.250
He was my neighbor and sat in front of me at school.

01:08:58.250 --> 01:09:00.280
That kinda friends, huh?

01:09:00.280 --> 01:09:01.900
It's not like that.

01:09:01.900 --> 01:09:03.940
I can see why you're worried.

01:09:03.940 --> 01:09:05.440
It's not like that.

01:09:14.900 --> 01:09:17.020
Did you eat this all by yourself?

01:09:20.230 --> 01:09:22.200
Huh? There's still more.

01:09:23.700 --> 01:09:26.370
I was actually tailing you first.

01:09:27.380 --> 01:09:28.100
Why?

01:09:28.100 --> 01:09:29.700
Because I was worried.

01:09:29.700 --> 01:09:31.680
What if something bad happened?

01:09:31.680 --> 01:09:33.140
I mean, you were almost kidnapped!

01:09:33.140 --> 01:09:34.250
I was not!

01:09:34.250 --> 01:09:36.880
That's why I said almost.

01:09:37.300 --> 01:09:38.930
You were worried about me?

01:09:38.930 --> 01:09:41.530
You're a good person, for a shut-in.

01:09:41.530 --> 01:09:43.440
I don't stay inside because I want to.

01:09:47.380 --> 01:09:48.940
It's pretty late.

01:09:48.940 --> 01:09:51.030
What do we do? We'll miss the train!

01:09:52.130 --> 01:09:56.270
I guess we can stop here for today. We know where they live now.

01:09:57.330 --> 01:09:59.100
We can come back.

01:09:59.100 --> 01:10:03.560
Boo. We got so close, too.

01:10:03.560 --> 01:10:05.130
Maybe he's already home.

01:10:05.130 --> 01:10:07.780
Just shout, "Kotaro Yuda, get out here!"

01:10:07.780 --> 01:10:09.090
He might stick his head out the window.

01:10:09.090 --> 01:10:11.200
Stop it. Please.

01:10:11.970 --> 01:10:15.470
What if everyone in the complex looks out the window?

01:10:19.260 --> 01:10:20.240
Found one!

01:10:28.650 --> 01:10:30.700
So cold.

01:10:30.700 --> 01:10:32.940
I'm turning to ice.

01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:35.010
I'm so hungry.

01:10:35.010 --> 01:10:37.540
Yeah, we haven't eaten anything today.

01:10:38.370 --> 01:10:39.960
There's a ramen shop!

01:10:39.960 --> 01:10:41.810
Yes, yes!

01:10:43.720 --> 01:10:45.620
Welcome!

01:10:45.620 --> 01:10:47.000
Sweet warmth!

01:10:47.000 --> 01:10:49.200
I almost froze.

01:10:49.660 --> 01:10:50.500
What to order...

01:10:50.500 --> 01:10:52.930
We're short on time. I'll have plain ramen.

01:10:52.930 --> 01:10:53.600
Mister!

01:10:53.600 --> 01:10:54.290
Yes?

01:10:54.290 --> 01:10:56.400
One plain and one miso with green onions!

01:10:56.400 --> 01:10:57.280
Coming up!

01:10:57.280 --> 01:10:59.770
I haven't eaten out in forever.

01:10:59.770 --> 01:11:00.930
Oh, right.

01:11:01.340 --> 01:11:03.110
It'd suck if the food's bad here.

01:11:03.110 --> 01:11:05.110
Oh my God, I know, right?

01:11:06.370 --> 01:11:07.850
Oh my God...

01:11:07.850 --> 01:11:09.410
Welcome!

01:11:07.850 --> 01:11:09.890
This place looks good.

01:11:11.280 --> 01:11:12.230
You sit there.

01:11:12.230 --> 01:11:13.430
Excuse me.

01:11:13.430 --> 01:11:14.360
You sit here.

01:11:14.360 --> 01:11:14.870
Okay.

01:11:15.460 --> 01:11:16.950
That was close.

01:11:16.950 --> 01:11:17.910
Why?

01:11:17.910 --> 01:11:20.370
If we got here after them, we'd be waiting forever.

01:11:20.850 --> 01:11:21.630
Good point.

01:11:21.630 --> 01:11:22.120
Yeah.

01:11:22.120 --> 01:11:24.240
I ordered for everyone already.

01:11:24.240 --> 01:11:25.300
Thanks!

01:11:25.300 --> 01:11:26.710
All right, barbecue pork ramen!

01:11:26.710 --> 01:11:29.290
That was fast. Man, look at the size of that pork.

01:11:30.480 --> 01:11:31.460
What now?

01:11:32.110 --> 01:11:35.950
We'll be cutting it close. Too risky.

01:11:35.950 --> 01:11:37.730
Guess we just leave.

01:11:38.210 --> 01:11:39.790
Excuse me!

01:11:39.250 --> 01:11:40.260
Yes?

01:11:39.790 --> 01:11:42.050
We have to go. Can we cancel?

01:11:42.050 --> 01:11:43.440
I've already started on yours.

01:11:44.100 --> 01:11:44.700
What now?

01:11:44.700 --> 01:11:46.270
What'd you order?

01:11:46.270 --> 01:11:49.250
If you want pork and green onions, I'll give you mine.

01:11:49.440 --> 01:11:52.170
I can trade you my fried liver set, too.

01:11:52.170 --> 01:11:53.290
What'd you girls order?

01:11:53.290 --> 01:11:55.470
No, no! Let us handle this!

01:11:55.470 --> 01:11:56.890
Hey, gimme yours!

01:11:56.890 --> 01:11:57.820
Hey!

01:11:57.820 --> 01:11:59.770
Are you serious, man?

01:11:59.770 --> 01:12:01.760
That's one. Enjoy.

01:12:01.760 --> 01:12:03.480
Lucky, huh?

01:12:03.480 --> 01:12:04.830
What do you say, girls?

01:12:04.830 --> 01:12:06.010
Thank you.

01:12:06.010 --> 01:12:07.810
Thank you very much.

01:12:06.440 --> 01:12:07.810
Gyoza, up!

01:12:07.810 --> 01:12:08.890
Let's eat!

01:12:08.890 --> 01:12:10.300
Have some gyoza, too!

01:12:10.300 --> 01:12:13.370
Thank you!

01:12:13.370 --> 01:12:14.070
Lucky again!

01:12:14.070 --> 01:12:15.160
Thank you very much!

01:12:15.160 --> 01:12:16.180
Eat up, eat up!

01:12:16.800 --> 01:12:17.360
You're so slow!

01:12:17.360 --> 01:12:19.120
You're too fast!

01:12:19.120 --> 01:12:20.640
Hurry up!

01:12:23.840 --> 01:12:24.610
What line?

01:12:24.940 --> 01:12:25.490
How much?

01:12:25.490 --> 01:12:27.420
Which line goes to Fujiko?

01:12:27.420 --> 01:12:28.650
Abiko? Fujimoto?{repeat}

01:12:28.650 --> 01:12:30.250
Abiko? Fujimoto? Abiko? Fujimoto?

01:12:30.250 --> 01:12:31.690
We don't have time for this!

01:12:31.690 --> 01:12:33.610
Which goes to Fujiko?

01:12:35.000 --> 01:12:37.330
The last train! No!

01:12:46.570 --> 01:12:48.000
Cold.

01:12:48.860 --> 01:12:50.630
So cold.

01:12:53.060 --> 01:12:54.490
A convenience store!

01:12:54.490 --> 01:12:56.730
Let's warm up in here.

01:12:57.760 --> 01:12:59.000
What's going on?

01:13:02.240 --> 01:13:02.980
No way.

01:13:03.430 --> 01:13:04.650
What the hell?

01:13:10.290 --> 01:13:13.280
We're stuck outside. What do we do now?

01:13:13.770 --> 01:13:16.420
Freeze to death till morning.

01:13:16.420 --> 01:13:17.980
I don't mind.

01:13:17.980 --> 01:13:19.800
Stop that!

01:13:19.800 --> 01:13:22.560
You might not, but I do!

01:13:25.050 --> 01:13:28.400
Hey, I never asked. Why don't you leave the house?

01:13:28.400 --> 01:13:29.610
Bullies?

01:13:30.580 --> 01:13:31.940
No.

01:13:42.740 --> 01:13:45.240
And we're back here again.

01:13:46.940 --> 01:13:48.430
Yuda!

01:13:48.430 --> 01:13:51.450
Hey! Stop that!

01:13:51.450 --> 01:13:52.890
I won't do it!

01:13:52.890 --> 01:13:56.200
You just did!

01:14:13.960 --> 01:14:16.280
Hey! What're you doing?

01:14:18.740 --> 01:14:20.410
We're gonna get caught.

01:14:20.410 --> 01:14:22.820
It's so warm.

01:14:22.820 --> 01:14:23.790
Really?

01:14:29.910 --> 01:14:31.290
Warmth!

01:14:34.020 --> 01:14:36.450
This is heaven!

01:14:40.160 --> 01:14:42.280
If Yuda's really dead...

01:14:43.210 --> 01:14:45.080
I'm the one who killed him.

01:14:45.770 --> 01:14:46.610
Huh?

01:14:49.300 --> 01:14:52.550
Want to know what happened?

01:14:53.170 --> 01:14:56.800
I'm not so sure anymore.

01:14:58.380 --> 01:15:03.640
For Valentine's Day I'd always give Yuda chocolate. Nothing special.

01:15:03.640 --> 01:15:06.580
We'd known each other since kindergarten.

01:15:06.580 --> 01:15:10.800
I always gave him chocolate for his birthday and Valentine's.

01:15:11.560 --> 01:15:17.440
And until third grade, he'd always return the favor.

01:15:17.440 --> 01:15:20.280
But in fourth grade he stopped.

01:15:20.280 --> 01:15:22.340
I was kinda sad.

01:15:22.960 --> 01:15:26.040
But you don't give presents to get presents, right?

01:15:26.040 --> 01:15:30.150
So I kept giving him chocolate like a good person.

01:15:31.180 --> 01:15:33.810
But in seventh grade,

01:15:33.810 --> 01:15:38.270
I prepared a special surprise and gave it to him with the chocolate.

01:15:39.570 --> 01:15:41.630
An envelope.

01:15:41.630 --> 01:15:43.550
Can you guess the contents?

01:15:44.210 --> 01:15:45.390
A love letter?

01:15:45.390 --> 01:15:46.680
Nope.

01:15:47.520 --> 01:15:48.480
A marriage license.

01:15:51.080 --> 01:15:52.310
A marriage license?

01:15:52.740 --> 01:15:56.330
I was basically saying that I hoped one day we'd sign it.

01:15:56.330 --> 01:15:58.080
Romantic, right?

01:15:58.080 --> 01:16:01.530
Uh, I dunno.

01:16:01.530 --> 01:16:03.420
What'd he say?

01:16:04.370 --> 01:16:05.660
He was stone-faced.

01:16:05.660 --> 01:16:07.620
Creeped out, huh?

01:16:07.620 --> 01:16:09.810
Maybe I wasn't clear enough.

01:16:09.810 --> 01:16:12.700
I didn't mean we had to get married right away.

01:16:12.700 --> 01:16:15.040
Zero need to feel pressured, right?

01:16:15.440 --> 01:16:18.300
But in the spring of ninth grade, something crazy happened!

01:16:18.300 --> 01:16:20.690
We were in the same class for once!

01:16:20.690 --> 01:16:23.530
And I was right behind him!

01:16:24.720 --> 01:16:30.690
That was the happiest day of my life.

01:16:36.360 --> 01:16:37.160
So?

01:16:39.170 --> 01:16:40.440
Did you kill him?

01:16:42.270 --> 01:16:43.970
Not yet.

01:16:48.100 --> 01:16:51.070
If he hadn't been an idiot,

01:16:51.520 --> 01:16:54.100
he wouldn't have forced my hand.

01:16:55.290 --> 01:16:58.230
Yuda, what'd you want to talk about?

01:16:59.360 --> 01:17:02.490
Do you like me?

01:17:03.630 --> 01:17:07.360
If you want me to be your girlfriend, I can do that.

01:17:07.360 --> 01:17:09.290
Then the deal's sealed.

01:17:10.620 --> 01:17:12.180
Can you sign this?

01:17:14.940 --> 01:17:16.210
What is this?

01:17:16.740 --> 01:17:18.250
Are you messing with me?

01:17:19.330 --> 01:17:20.390
Bastard!

01:18:02.760 --> 01:18:04.410
That's not your name.

01:18:05.320 --> 01:18:07.510
It is. The marriage changed it.

01:18:07.510 --> 01:18:08.750
What?

01:18:08.750 --> 01:18:09.670
Who married?

01:18:09.670 --> 01:18:10.960
Your parents?

01:18:10.960 --> 01:18:12.140
Me.

01:18:14.250 --> 01:18:16.330
Excuse me.

01:18:19.200 --> 01:18:21.490
Who got married, now?

01:18:21.490 --> 01:18:22.880
Me.

01:18:23.580 --> 01:18:24.760
To whom?

01:18:28.440 --> 01:18:29.430
Yuda.

01:18:30.580 --> 01:18:32.310
What's the matter, Kijima?

01:18:32.820 --> 01:18:34.780
There must be a mistake.

01:18:34.780 --> 01:18:37.270
He's married to me!

01:18:39.040 --> 01:18:40.900
Was I tricked, then?

01:18:46.160 --> 01:18:47.690
Arai!

01:18:50.540 --> 01:18:53.660
Honestly. Yuda ran away from me.

01:18:53.660 --> 01:18:56.260
Now I have to pay his parents a visit.

01:18:56.260 --> 01:18:58.420
He's been a little off recently, no?

01:18:58.420 --> 01:19:01.370
Maybe it's just puberty. What do you think?

01:19:02.050 --> 01:19:03.250
Dunno.

01:19:05.230 --> 01:19:07.770
You're neighbors, right? Aren't you friends?

01:19:07.770 --> 01:19:10.630
Just because we're neighbors doesn't mean we're friends.

01:19:11.120 --> 01:19:13.490
You sit behind him.

01:19:16.530 --> 01:19:19.190
Did he not propose to you?

01:19:21.610 --> 01:19:22.700
No.

01:19:41.630 --> 01:19:43.250
Stand!

01:19:46.850 --> 01:19:47.970
Bow!

01:19:50.120 --> 01:19:51.600
Be seated.

01:19:53.060 --> 01:19:54.600
Okay, everyone.

01:19:54.600 --> 01:19:57.220
I have a bit of sad news.

01:19:57.890 --> 01:20:02.270
Yuda's family is going to be moving, so he has to transfer.

01:20:02.830 --> 01:20:05.670
Come on, Yuda. Say something to everyone.

01:20:05.280 --> 01:20:06.080
Really?

01:20:06.080 --> 01:20:07.310
No way.

01:20:09.450 --> 01:20:12.630
I'm Yuda, and I'll be transferring soon.

01:20:12.630 --> 01:20:18.170
I know I did some bad things. Just forget about me.

01:20:18.170 --> 01:20:20.790
Have a fun life without me.

01:20:20.790 --> 01:20:21.490
Thanks.

01:20:23.220 --> 01:20:25.380
What's wrong, Yuda?

01:20:25.940 --> 01:20:27.170
Yuda!

01:20:28.180 --> 01:20:29.490
You can die from a bee sting, dude!

01:20:29.490 --> 01:20:30.260
Seriously?

01:20:30.260 --> 01:20:31.580
Seriously. I saw it on TV.

01:20:31.580 --> 01:20:32.090
No way.

01:20:32.090 --> 01:20:34.540
You die from the shock. I forget what it's called.

01:20:34.130 --> 01:20:34.540
What?

01:20:34.540 --> 01:20:35.110
Ultrashock?

01:20:35.110 --> 01:20:36.490
Anaphylactic shock.

01:20:36.490 --> 01:20:37.200
Huh? What?

01:20:37.200 --> 01:20:38.450
What was that? Say it again.

01:20:38.450 --> 01:20:40.210
Anaphylactic shock.

01:20:45.680 --> 01:20:47.200
Are you Hana Arai?

01:20:47.200 --> 01:20:50.040
You're the one who put the bee down Yuda's shirt.

01:20:50.040 --> 01:20:51.850
You're under arrest for murder.

01:20:57.520 --> 01:21:05.140
I think a "bee" appears before every criminal right before they commit the crime.

01:21:05.760 --> 01:21:07.000
Don't you think?

01:21:07.000 --> 01:21:10.090
I dunno.

01:21:10.810 --> 01:21:13.620
That's all you say.

01:21:16.540 --> 01:21:19.560
Is that why you stopped going to school?

01:21:22.360 --> 01:21:23.390
If he's...

01:21:31.510 --> 01:21:33.000
really dead...

01:21:39.580 --> 01:21:41.500
then I killed him.

01:21:48.790 --> 01:21:50.270
I...

01:21:51.720 --> 01:21:53.060
might have...

01:22:00.450 --> 01:22:02.540
murdered someone.

01:22:11.430 --> 01:22:13.780
When I think of that, I...

01:22:20.540 --> 01:22:22.990
I can't sleep.

01:22:28.180 --> 01:22:29.940
Before I knew it...

01:22:35.100 --> 01:22:40.210
I couldn't even leave the house.

01:22:52.210 --> 01:22:53.470
She's crying.

01:23:02.920 --> 01:23:04.270
My leg's cramping.

01:23:05.010 --> 01:23:06.930
You're pretty good for a beginner.

01:23:06.930 --> 01:23:09.020
You're not even looking at me.

01:23:09.020 --> 01:23:11.600
I can just tell.

01:23:17.100 --> 01:23:18.720
Hey, look. Tons of stars.

01:23:31.890 --> 01:23:34.120
What dance is that?

01:23:35.410 --> 01:23:37.170
<i>Sleeping Beauty.</i>

01:23:39.070 --> 01:23:40.240
How's that story go?

01:23:41.600 --> 01:23:43.730
Let me see...

01:23:43.730 --> 01:23:46.040
It's about a princess that gets stung by a bee.

01:23:46.040 --> 01:23:46.900
What?

01:23:46.900 --> 01:23:48.710
Just kidding!

01:23:49.160 --> 01:23:50.560
Come on.

01:23:52.480 --> 01:23:55.340
She's nailed to a wall and trapped forever.

01:23:55.340 --> 01:23:56.420
What?!

01:23:56.850 --> 01:23:58.820
Just kidding!

01:23:58.820 --> 01:24:01.930
Ow! Ow!

01:24:39.940 --> 01:24:41.450
Someone's coming.

01:24:41.450 --> 01:24:42.240
Huh?

01:24:51.420 --> 01:24:52.070
Huh?

01:24:52.690 --> 01:24:54.330
I think they're going to sleep.

01:24:54.330 --> 01:24:57.370
With the engine on? Talk about rude.

01:25:05.190 --> 01:25:07.080
So warmsies.

01:25:07.080 --> 01:25:09.680
It's heaven on Earthsies.

01:25:09.680 --> 01:25:11.860
And spacious, toosies.

01:25:12.250 --> 01:25:16.250
With a bathroom, I could live heresies.

01:25:18.740 --> 01:25:22.490
You think Yuda's alive?

01:25:23.020 --> 01:25:25.430
I hope so.

01:25:29.160 --> 01:25:29.560
Ow!

01:25:33.340 --> 01:25:35.500
My head...

01:25:37.260 --> 01:25:39.630
Whoa, it's 7:30!

01:25:39.630 --> 01:25:41.060
Hey, you!

01:25:41.060 --> 01:25:42.220
Get up!

01:25:42.220 --> 01:25:45.490
We have to get to our post!

01:25:46.370 --> 01:25:49.130
No use. She's dead to the world.

01:25:50.840 --> 01:25:54.580
Fine, I'll go myself.

01:26:28.050 --> 01:26:29.540
Hana?

01:26:29.540 --> 01:26:30.790
Hana, where are you?

01:26:32.150 --> 01:26:33.160
Hana?

01:26:48.360 --> 01:26:50.970
Hana!

01:26:54.880 --> 01:26:57.020
Alice?

01:26:59.840 --> 01:27:02.760
Hana!

01:27:06.870 --> 01:27:08.450
What <i>is</i> she doing?

01:27:15.090 --> 01:27:16.340
Hana!

01:27:16.340 --> 01:27:17.020
Hey!

01:27:17.020 --> 01:27:19.370
Stop that truck!

01:27:19.370 --> 01:27:20.290
Ow!

01:27:20.290 --> 01:27:22.500
What's your problem?

01:27:33.850 --> 01:27:37.620
My friend's being dragged by that truck!

01:27:54.810 --> 01:27:56.730
Someone's being dragged by a truck!

01:27:56.730 --> 01:27:58.410
Someone's being dragged by a truck!

01:28:03.920 --> 01:28:08.120
Whoa, whoa, whoa! What's she doing?

01:28:14.180 --> 01:28:16.090
Stop!{repeat}

01:28:19.840 --> 01:28:21.890
What's wrong with you? That's dangerous!

01:28:21.890 --> 01:28:24.060
There's a person stuck under there!

01:28:24.060 --> 01:28:26.680
There! Over there!

01:28:29.960 --> 01:28:31.670
Alice!

01:28:31.670 --> 01:28:33.720
What? Where?

01:28:33.720 --> 01:28:34.830
What?

01:28:38.700 --> 01:28:39.660
Alice?

01:28:44.440 --> 01:28:46.450
Where were you?

01:28:47.350 --> 01:28:48.960
Yuda's house.

01:28:48.960 --> 01:28:51.420
You wouldn't wake up.

01:28:51.420 --> 01:28:54.220
So I went to watch alone.

01:28:54.880 --> 01:28:55.970
What?

01:28:55.970 --> 01:28:57.480
What's up?

01:28:58.540 --> 01:29:00.270
What?

01:29:00.270 --> 01:29:01.870
What's the matter?

01:29:14.690 --> 01:29:16.260
Someone got run over by a truck!

01:29:16.260 --> 01:29:17.640
No way!

01:29:20.200 --> 01:29:24.160
I think I figured out what you did.

01:29:24.790 --> 01:29:27.630
You've cursed me! I'm going home!

01:29:28.020 --> 01:29:30.510
I don't care if Yuda's alive or dead!

01:29:39.560 --> 01:29:40.720
What?

01:29:45.040 --> 01:29:46.880
What? What happened?

01:29:46.880 --> 01:29:48.240
That was Yuda.

01:29:48.240 --> 01:29:48.800
Huh?

01:29:48.800 --> 01:29:50.770
Yuda's alive.

01:29:51.210 --> 01:29:52.440
What?

01:30:09.690 --> 01:30:12.790
That uniform looks terrible on him.

01:30:15.780 --> 01:30:18.540
Is he really still using that bag?

01:30:22.940 --> 01:30:24.180
Yuda!

01:30:28.370 --> 01:30:30.160
Yuda!

01:30:30.160 --> 01:30:31.860
I really will kill you.

01:30:32.500 --> 01:30:34.070
Who're you?

01:30:34.920 --> 01:30:36.160
What're you doing?

01:30:36.160 --> 01:30:38.280
Let go!

01:30:39.370 --> 01:30:42.280
My friend wants to talk to you.

01:30:42.280 --> 01:30:43.600
Not!

01:30:45.130 --> 01:30:46.300
What?

01:30:56.400 --> 01:30:57.340
Hana.

01:30:59.900 --> 01:31:01.320
Hi.

01:31:02.510 --> 01:31:03.370
Hey.

01:31:04.620 --> 01:31:06.110
How've you been?

01:31:07.180 --> 01:31:08.560
Okay.

01:31:08.560 --> 01:31:09.710
I see.

01:31:10.920 --> 01:31:11.770
Bye.

01:31:12.190 --> 01:31:13.210
Wait, what? That's all?

01:31:13.210 --> 01:31:15.570
Say something else!

01:31:16.100 --> 01:31:16.650
Hana.

01:31:21.570 --> 01:31:24.050
You put the bee down my shirt, right?

01:31:24.580 --> 01:31:26.070
That really hurt.

01:31:26.490 --> 01:31:27.870
I'll never forget it.

01:31:32.780 --> 01:31:34.360
Hana!

01:31:45.350 --> 01:31:46.520
Hey.

01:31:46.520 --> 01:31:48.850
Why'd you run off like that?

01:31:48.850 --> 01:31:52.510
What else do you do when someone says that?

01:31:53.320 --> 01:31:56.190
He was basically confessing his eternal love.

01:31:56.190 --> 01:31:57.450
Why?

01:31:57.450 --> 01:32:01.510
"I'll never forget that pain."

01:32:02.680 --> 01:32:05.950
He's, like, head-over-heels for me!

01:32:06.820 --> 01:32:08.360
Really?

01:32:12.820 --> 01:32:15.010
Don't say anything.

01:32:15.780 --> 01:32:18.160
I don't care if I'm deluding myself.

01:32:18.550 --> 01:32:21.700
I just want to lose myself in this happiness.

01:32:25.260 --> 01:32:26.750
She's gone.

01:32:32.870 --> 01:32:33.850
What?

01:32:33.850 --> 01:32:36.410
Is this how you wear a sailor suit?

01:32:36.410 --> 01:32:38.900
Why not? Everyone has their own way.

01:32:40.280 --> 01:32:41.500
Hana.

01:32:42.140 --> 01:32:43.680
Where are you going?

01:32:44.520 --> 01:32:45.980
Where?

01:32:46.600 --> 01:32:47.980
School.

01:32:50.860 --> 01:32:52.210
Hana...

01:33:09.190 --> 01:33:11.200
First day in a sailor suit, huh?

01:33:11.900 --> 01:33:14.210
They finally got one in stock.

01:33:14.210 --> 01:33:16.280
First day in a long time for you, too.

01:33:16.280 --> 01:33:18.410
One year, four months.

01:33:22.400 --> 01:33:25.080
Looks lame!

01:33:22.400 --> 01:33:25.080
Looks lame!

01:33:27.910 --> 01:33:29.440
Let's get to school!

